## 1. Introduction

This guide outlines the process for creating list components using the uu5Generate command.

### 1.1 When to Use

Use this guide when creating components for:
- Entity list views (e.g., Library List, Note List)
- Collections with filtering and sorting capabilities
- Paginated data display with actions

### 1.2 Fundamental Rule

⚠️ **ABSOLUTE MANDATORY REQUIREMENT** ⚠️

**NO IMPLEMENTATION BEFORE USER CONFIRMATION - ZERO EXCEPTIONS!**

Before writing ANY code, you MUST ALWAYS:

1. 🛑 STOP and ASK the user to specify:
   - Module name (e.g., `Note`, `Library`)
   - Component name (e.g., `List`, `VersionTagList`)
   - Object/entity description or uuSchema documentation link

2. 🛑 WAIT for explicit user confirmation before proceeding.

3. 🛑 DO NOT proceed with ANY implementation until you have received clear specifications.

> **LIST COMPONENT RULE**  
> When a user wants to create a new **list component**, do NOT generate any files manually.  
> Instead, use the uu5Generate command in the **-core library**:
> ```bash
> npm run uu5Generate listComponent <module>.<name> -- --sub-app=<value> --brick-uu5-tag=<value> --redirect-uu5-route=<value>
> ```


**⚠️ WARNING**: NEVER call uu5Generate without ALL parameters - it will prompt for interactive input!

**IMPORTANT**: ALWAYS use cmd when calling uu5Generate. Do NOT use PowerShell as it causes syntax issues with the command execution.

