## 3. Generation Process

### 3.1 Command Parameters

**Optional Parameters** (with default values):
> • **sub-app** [string] – the sub app of the corresponding uuApp  
>   *Default: derived from library name (e.g. `uu_frontend_aicodingg01-core` → `uu_frontend_aicodingg01`)*  
>   *This option is **mandatory** for all cases*
> • **brick-uu5-tag** [string] – full uu5Tag of related brick component for "Copy component" functionality  
>   *Default: `"-"` (taken as empty when used)*  
>   *This option is **mandatory** when generate-brick is positive*
> • **generate-brick** [bool] – whether to generate related brick component  
>   *This is a **mandatory** option with no default value*  
>   *Use `no-generate-brick` when user doesn't want to generate brick component*
> • **redirect-uu5-route** [string] – related uu5Route for "Redirect / open in new window" functionality  
>   *Default: `"-"`*
> 
> **Process**:
> 1. **ALWAYS provide ALL parameters** when calling uu5Generate - never call it without parameters
> 2. **Use default values** for all parameters unless user specifies otherwise
> 3. **Execute the uu5Generate command** with ALL parameters specified
> 
> **CRITICAL**: NEVER call `npm run uu5Generate listComponent <module>.<name>` without parameters. ALWAYS include all required parameters: `--sub-app`, `--brick-uu5-tag`, and `--redirect-uu5-route`.
> 
> **Examples**:
> ```bash
> # CORRECT: Using default values (all parameters MUST be specified)
> # ALWAYS use cmd, NOT PowerShell
> cmd /c "npm run uu5Generate listComponent Note.List -- --sub-app=uu_frontend_aicodingg01 --brick-uu5-tag=- --redirect-uu5-route=-"
> 
> # CORRECT: Overriding specific parameters
> cmd /c "npm run uu5Generate listComponent Note.List -- --sub-app=mySubApp --brick-uu5-tag=UuMyAppBricks.Note.List --redirect-uu5-route=noteList"
> 
> # CORRECT: When not generating brick component
> cmd /c "npm run uu5Generate listComponent Note.List -- --sub-app=uu_frontend_aicodingg01 --no-generate-brick --redirect-uu5-route=-"
> 
> # WRONG: Never call without parameters - this will prompt for input
> # npm run uu5Generate listComponent Note.List
> ```
> 
> The uu5Generate command will automatically create all necessary files including:
> - Component files (js, test, html demo)
> - Proper ContentContainer integration
> - Registration in uuapp.json
- Brick component generation (if applicable)

### 3.2 Object Description
> After the list component is successfully generated, you MUST check if the user already provided object documentation in their initial request. If they did, use that information directly. If not, ask the user for the object that will be represented by the list component.
> 
> **Check first**: Look for uuSchema documentation links or object descriptions in the user's initial prompt
> 
> **If not provided, ask the user to provide**:
> • **Object Description** – Either a text description of the object/entity that the list component will represent, OR
> • **Documentation Link** – A link to the uuSchema documentation that describes the object structure
> 
> **Purpose**: This information will be used to:
> - Implement the content component with proper data fields
> - Configure the component's data mapping
> - Set up appropriate validation and business logic
> - Create meaningful demo data
> 
> **Example questions to ask**:
> - "What object/entity will this list component represent? Please provide either a text description or a link to the uuSchema documentation."
> - "What data fields and properties should this list component display for the [Module] entity?"
- "Do you have a uuSchema documentation link that describes the structure of the [Module] object?"

## 4. SeriesList Configuration

### 4.1 SeriesList Structure
> After receiving the object description, you MUST configure the seriesList prop based on the object attributes. The seriesList defines the columns/fields that will be displayed in the list component.
> 
> **SeriesList Format**:
> The seriesList is an array of objects with the following structure:
> ```javascript
> function getSerieList(viewLsi) {
>   return [
>     {
>       value: "fieldName",
>       label: viewLsi.fieldLabel,
>       dataItem: ({ data: entityDto }) => entityDto.data.fieldName,
>     },
>     // ... more fields
>   ];
> }
> ```
> 
> **Configuration Process**:
> 1. **Map object attributes** to seriesList items based on the object description
> 2. **Add LSI labels** for each field in the LSI file
> 3. **Update the getSerieList function** in `src/[module]/list/view.js`
> 4. **Configure dataItem functions** to extract the correct data from entityDto.data
> 
**Purpose**: The seriesList prop defines the columns/fields that will be displayed in the list component, mapping object attributes to display labels and data extraction functions.

### 4.2 List Command Verification
> After receiving the seriesList description, you MUST check the provided documentation for the list command to verify the correct parameters and structure.
> 
> **Primary verification - List command**:
> - Look for the `[module]/list` command in the documentation (e.g., `library/list`)
> - Verify what parameters are used in `dtoIn` (e.g., `pageInfo`, `sortOrder`, `filterMap`)
> - Check the command signature to confirm the expected input parameters
> - Verify the response structure and what data is returned
> 
**Purpose**: This ensures the list component is configured with the correct command parameters and can properly handle the list data.

### 4.3 Object ID Configuration
> Based on the list command documentation, configure the correct identifier attribute. If the command uses `id` instead of `oid`, you MUST:
> 
> 1. **Change `oid` prop to `id`** in the main list component (`src/[module]/list.js`)
> 2. **Change `oid` prop to `id`** in the provider component (`src/[module]/provider.js`)
> 3. **Change `oid` prop to `id`** in the use-provider hook (`src/[module]/use-provider.js`)
> 4. **Update propTypes** to use `id` instead of `oid` in all affected components
> 5. **Update the provider propTypes** to reflect the correct identifier field
> 6. **Update the demo page** (`demo/[module]/list.html`) to use the correct identifier:
>    - Change the `oid` prop to the correct identifier (e.g., `id`, `code`)
>    - Update any hardcoded demo values to use the correct identifier format
   - Ensure the demo page works with the new identifier structure

### 4.4 BaseUri Configuration
> After configuring the object ID, you MUST ask the user about baseUri configuration:
> 
> **Ask the user**:
> - "Will the baseUri be the same for workspace check and for the [Module] object loading?"
> - "If different, what baseUri should be used for [Module] object loading?"
> - "Do you want to remove the WorkspaceProvider and use only baseUri for [Module] object loading? (workspace state check is not needed)"
> 
> **Purpose**: This determines whether to use the same baseUri for both workspace validation and object data loading, or if separate baseUris are needed for different operations.
> 
> **Implementation options**:
> - **Option 1 - Same baseUri**: Use the existing `baseUri` prop for both workspace and object operations
> - **Option 2 - Different baseUri**: Define TWO separate props:
>   - `baseUri` - for workspace check operations
>   - `objectBaseUri` - for object loading operations
>   - **Update the list component** to pass the correct baseUri to each provider:
>     - `baseUri` prop → passed to `WorkspaceProvider` as `baseUri`
>     - `objectBaseUri` prop → passed to `[Module]Provider` as `baseUri`
> - **Option 3 - Remove WorkspaceProvider**: Remove WorkspaceProvider entirely and use only baseUri for [Module] object loading:
>   - Remove `WorkspaceProvider` import and usage from list component
>   - Pass `baseUri` directly to `[Module]Provider`
>   - Update propTypes to use `[Module]Provider.propTypes.baseUri` instead of `WorkspaceProvider.propTypes.baseUri`
>   - **Clean up unused workspace components**: If WorkspaceProvider is not used elsewhere, delete the generated workspace-related files:
>     - `src/workspace/workspace.js`
>     - `src/workspace/config/config.js`
>     - `src/workspace/provider.js`
>     - `src/workspace/use-workspace.js`
>     - Remove workspace-related calls from `src/calls.js`
>     - Remove workspace exports from `src/exports.js` and `src/index.js`
>   - **Update demo pages**: When removing WorkspaceProvider, the demo pages need to be updated:
>     - Move `baseUri` prop from `Plus4U5.SpaProvider` to components directly
>     - Update `demo/[module]/list.html` to pass `baseUri` prop to the list component
>     - Remove workspace-related data from ContentContainer dataMap
    - Update inlineView dataToResolve to remove workspace dependency

